        {
          "type": "blockContainer",
          "attrs": { "id": "d108f958-c41f-4152-a19c-746e77a9cb01" },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "attrs": {
                "backgroundColor": "default",
                "textColor": "default",
                "textAlignment": "left",
                "level": 2,
                "isToggleable": false
              },
              "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Rationale" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockContainer",
          "attrs": { "id": "68e972d1-70ee-4ebf-a037-5147e4842ad7" },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "backgroundColor": "default",
                "textColor": "default",
                "textAlignment": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }], "text": "Why TTL-only?" },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " Mutation volume (album updates, member joins/leaves) is low relative to reads. A 60 s stale window is acceptable. Explicit invalidation would require touching every mutating function across albums, members, and join-requests modules — far more surface area."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockContainer",
          "attrs": { "id": "317ade31-8ef9-49b7-b4c1-bd7653df70f5" },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "backgroundColor": "default",
                "textColor": "default",
                "textAlignment": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }],
                  "text": "Why a thin cache adapter instead of using ioredis directly?"
                },
                { "type": "text", "text": " (a) No-op fallback when " },
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "code" }], "text": "REDIS_URL" },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " is absent; (b) one place for JSON serialization and silent error handling. Intentionally minimal — no key-prefix registry, no generics tower."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockContainer",
          "attrs": { "id": "ba5b5da2-5cdd-4288-ba19-2f7d6b3f2d62" },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "backgroundColor": "default",
                "textColor": "default",
                "textAlignment": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }], "text": "Why not cache " },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }, { "type": "code" }],
                  "text": "listAlbums"
                },
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }], "text": " or " },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }, { "type": "code" }],
                  "text": "getAlbumDetail"
                },
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }], "text": "?" },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " Both are per-user aggregates. With TTL-only strategy, a 60 s stale count on the home screen is more noticeable. Leaving for a follow-up if needed."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockContainer",
          "attrs": { "id": "b1657b17-580d-4465-ae6c-77592547b320" },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
                "backgroundColor": "default",
                "textColor": "default",
                "textAlignment": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }], "text": "Deletion test:" },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " if deleted in 6 months, the API falls back to Supabase on every request — no data corruption, just slower. Complexity only reappears if Redis is removed without reverting the env schema."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockContainer",
          "attrs": { "id": "833d7bef-1c72-4579-b1c8-9edd38e6bb5f" },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "attrs": {
                "backgroundColor": "default",
                "textColor": "default",
                "textAlignment": "left",
                "level": 2,
                "isToggleable": false
              },
              "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Uncertainties" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockContainer",
          "attrs": { "id": "327b5fb1-cdf7-4ad3-8309-dd438a7ed1e9" },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "attrs": {
                "backgroundColor": "default",
                "textColor": "default",
                "textAlignment": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }],
                  "text": "ioredis + Bun compatibility:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " ioredis is Node-compatible and Bun supports Node APIs broadly, but not verified for this exact combo. Fallback: "
                },
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "code" }], "text": "redis" },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " (official Node client) has identical API shape for our use."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockContainer",
          "attrs": { "id": "63c1e06c-7f85-41ee-a3a4-b6f243e372cc" },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "attrs": {
                "backgroundColor": "default",
                "textColor": "default",
                "textAlignment": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }],
                  "text": "Railway Redis URL format:"
                },
                { "type": "text", "text": " Railway provides " },
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "code" }], "text": "redis://..." },
                { "type": "text", "text": " which ioredis accepts directly. If TLS is required (" },
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "code" }], "text": "rediss://" },
                { "type": "text", "text": "), the constructor needs " },
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "code" }], "text": "{ tls: {} }" },
                { "type": "text", "text": " — flagged but not yet confirmed." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockContainer",
          "attrs": { "id": "ec72ea0f-f080-44bb-b18d-0d6675d44c89" },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "bulletListItem",
              "attrs": {
                "backgroundColor": "default",
                "textColor": "default",
                "textAlignment": "left"
              },
              "content": [
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }], "text": "Silent error handling:" },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " Redis errors are logged and return null (cache miss), not thrown. A Redis outage degrades to uncached behavior. Intentional but worth noting."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
